{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/pages/cli.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:43:01.210379Z","id":"72ec55f5e128e50b5c536f7225f1573384c3d905ce44887f847d5cf0e36d3607","body":{"detail":"Pinned in crates/path-cli/tests/snapshots/cli_page_vs_binary.snap (test cli_surface::cli_page_vs_binary): the page lists none of config/config edit, p cache sync (which the home page's quick start uses), p render md, show/list/import/export/derive for most harnesses (only claude/git/pathbase appear), p incept claude|cursor, p project claude: 45 commands, plus 31 flags on 10 documented commands (e.g. share --harness/--session/--anon, resume --harness, query --no-sync/--project-under, export claude --session-id).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":24},"end":{"line":66},"content_hash":"cf859c3344b95cd7c28f58583c2efc8912d34f3deec2b94e673c0d8447d1c07e"},"summary":"The command tree omits most of the binary's commands","tags":["cli-surface","review","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/pages/cli.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:43:01.218877Z","id":"592634fb43b395aa915be899f61d558ad44cc53a5da70621c3c6d34aac2ab49e","body":{"detail":"The page marks [--force] [--no-cache] as global; the binary accepts them on p import <source> (and share/resume for --no-cache), not on every command (help snapshots help@*.snap).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":44},"end":{"line":44},"content_hash":"a4a3aa03ac6ac81f517c711eefacd3a6da6c5c3a994eeb5b2f01fff437817cc9"},"summary":"The --force and --no-cache flags are not global","tags":["cli-surface","review","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/pages/cli.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:43:01.225603Z","id":"8e52e17efb976a54a824c61e81423f1b6bca3286314a3234e7046b4fd4442321","body":{"detail":"The example steps use --session /tmp/session.json, but p track init writes $TMPDIR/track-<stamp>-<pid>.path.jsonl and prints that path; nothing creates /tmp/session.json. The workflow works when the printed path is used (behaviour@p-track.snap, test cli_surface::track_workflow_from_the_cli_page).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":141},"end":{"line":151},"content_hash":"84bf95617986c92c561e8324e7233232daac91f6f4a78bbf91a185d2261d7fe8"},"suggested_fix":"S=$(cat src/main.rs | path p track init …) then --session \"$S\"","summary":"The track workflow's session path does not match what track init does","tags":["cli-surface","review","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/pages/cli.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:43:01.233826Z","id":"6e5ea38b4658a28df3e4232b7d61912fc1e86a0a219063f5fd70f515849e53f0","body":{"detail":"RFC.md resolves parents and path.head within the containing path, but p validate reports Valid for a step with parents [missing] (behaviour@p-validate.snap). Schema-level errors (a step without actor) are rejected (exit 1). So structurally valid holds for the JSON Schema, not for reference integrity.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":171},"end":{"line":171},"content_hash":"a80fad3a3a00f5b2bca731a141d13fccb37dda28604cb52510f6fac386b1b8ed"},"summary":"p validate accepts a step whose parent does not exist","tags":["cli-surface","review","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/pages/cli.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:43:01.240050Z","id":"4696ef6156702fcf935704ed5bc5bc1dfa83203c5611b32e685e6c5d3f111acc","body":{"detail":"p merge and p query ancestors print object keys of change maps and structural changes in hash order, so the same input printed different bytes across two runs. The snapshots canonicalise JSON (canonical_json) to pin content; byte-stable output needs ordered maps in the serialised types.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":70},"end":{"line":70},"content_hash":"1df418796f14b9924d56c87daf197de8ff5aa44a725b85fdb6cb561d4014e9d2"},"summary":"JSON output key order is not deterministic","tags":["cli-surface","review","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/pages/cli.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:43:01.245852Z","id":"f4f6771023077b402013591ce2a8cce15d569a4e1a96d274d0b6f7d93349a47f","body":{"detail":"behaviour@p-import-git.snap over a deterministic two-branch repo: one Path for --branch main, a Graph with one Path per branch for two --branch flags (test cli_surface::import_git_single_and_multi_branch).","kind":"pass","span":{"start":{"line":114},"end":{"line":120},"content_hash":"b717eef760161acfef0644369a0217dc0b44f85ecb910a327119000ef7c0d17c"},"summary":"p import git and multi-branch import work as the page shows","tags":["cli-surface","review","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/pages/cli.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:43:01.252597Z","id":"0eb193ba648aa34c67eea7319cfc5778b847d8c478506e5258f04304b176ebd3","body":{"detail":"behaviour@p-merge.snap (test cli_surface::merge_and_render_dot).","kind":"pass","span":{"start":{"line":157},"end":{"line":163},"content_hash":"20c0b593d083f539ffd1653ff1ce11c024027c1230d8a8ce44a6f4071ed0b5fa"},"summary":"p merge combines documents into a Graph","tags":["cli-surface","review","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/pages/cli.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:43:01.259109Z","id":"169023733ac1874489b7280f70adc1d0125bb42b22ba9c1cb7ce9ad8fbbf574a","body":{"detail":"query --input examples/path-04-exploration.path.json map(select(.dead_end)) returns step-002a, the example's dead end (behaviour@query-exploration.snap). Needs --no-sync in a hermetic HOME; without it query first syncs the cache.","kind":"pass","span":{"start":{"line":130},"end":{"line":136},"content_hash":"e7ad741747785ec166f766168d16d84c3dfb692946f196707377801a8da78144"},"summary":"The dead-end query returns the steps outside the head's ancestry","tags":["cli-surface","review","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
