{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/pages/faq.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:31:49.699372Z","id":"15afb9c86b59a6eb6e446ffacb3321c5a74e2d7f217bc507f5b3f587fa9ae643","body":{"detail":"toolpath::v1::Base has a toolpath:<path>/<step> constructor (types::test_base_constructors) and the schema accepts any uri, but no code follows such a base to the other path's step; the RFC also says cross-path step references are not supported (for parents), so the two need one sentence reconciling them.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:04afa53","span":{"start":{"line":41},"end":{"line":41},"content_hash":"9c6798f3aba29685236a79a3a1a71d5b599ee4fba66359d4993f4a0df1ee4772"},"summary":"FAQ: a base can be a toolpath: URI to another path's step — constructible, nothing resolves it","tags":["claim:faq-toolpath-base-uri","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
