{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/pages/faq.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T18:38:48.770343Z","id":"1f8264af770e225db79963f6d3331bb41391f746fb4fcc49d5fb3e889c3a6e41","body":{"detail":"Agent sessions reuse the harness's own turn id and fall back to step-NNNN (toolpath-convo derive.rs:112-118); git uses step-<short oid> (toolpath-git). Record the de facto rule or choose one; the RFC's uniqueness rule is not enforced (rfc-id-uniqueness).","kind":"concern","ref":"git:04afa53","span":{"start":{"line":99},"end":{"line":99},"content_hash":"1050fcd8beaf810d57b3b46baf1828d0228123a3f79964a11430885fefb65c92"},"summary":"FAQ open question 'how should step IDs be generated?' — producers already decided in practice","supersedes":"56e62dd84c96ead5d6eddd86c91a705309c6e9e747999a944da3b077614dd449","tags":["claim:faq-open-step-ids","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/pages/faq.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T18:38:48.770739Z","id":"c3806b6aa1afd46f8ac2d8daac3d7a64b57ef28a7bd536e884e7c6b6c7457d43","body":{"detail":"Every structural.type producers write today: conversation.append, conversation.event, file.write (document@ snapshots); no core.* and no language AST ops.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:04afa53","span":{"start":{"line":103},"end":{"line":103},"content_hash":"765674ccdeae01acca35dd0d205d65c954f61e92b4a2ee0a0f5acf09b6708dce"},"summary":"FAQ open question 'who defines structural types?' — the types in use are not namespaced as leaned","supersedes":"acb700cfd8c435fd200cf35746ee28eab473b5e27797a7dc0885769f947115a7","tags":["claim:faq-open-structural-types","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/pages/faq.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T18:38:48.771068Z","id":"f6d3692495b4bdd7e7cf39988b23b2a3be8edf0c462ac3fb886b385f4719229c","body":{"detail":"Agent-session documents embed full text, reasoning and tool output; the only secret control is the no_secrets gate over committed fixtures (crates/toolpath-webmock tests/no_secrets.rs), not over documents users share.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:04afa53","span":{"start":{"line":107},"end":{"line":107},"content_hash":"9c78f1f27ffe878790428c15051bab3ea1265df3fd6b6fa6a94e5cd9a9651e61"},"summary":"FAQ open question 'privacy and redaction' — still open; no redaction marker exists","supersedes":"a6559ff1ff75386196aa77ac3ee7f287230f8cedaba2476b71a8e367df7d802f","tags":["claim:faq-open-privacy","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/pages/faq.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T18:39:07.729588Z","id":"a75e314a06b8fc2835161e5b7ec24ca5e7e73c57c48c522d5be34e33c85b6f7c","body":{"detail":"Moved out of Open design questions (it was stale: kinds already answer it). Each kind version ships its own schema at its own URI (crates/path-cli/kinds/agent-coding-session/<v>/schema.json, mirrored under site/kinds; kinds::parse_uri_extracts_name_and_version, bundled_kind_uris_parse); a superseded URI stays valid: cmd_validate::legacy_kind_warns_once_per_path_and_still_validates (v1.0.0 validates, with a warning). Same evidence as claim:kind-index-immutable (site/kinds/index.md:11). The v1.1.0 kind schema sets no additionalProperties: false, and validate@<set>.snap is valid for all 9 sets, so extra properties do not invalidate a path.","kind":"pass","ref":"git:f308ab5","span":{"start":{"line":85},"end":{"line":85},"content_hash":"beb034e288ac165f1bf7e726573a9faf76ffb2bf28eea4f82a8adf852889c567"},"summary":"FAQ: the format evolves through kinds — immutable, semver-versioned kind URIs; answered, no longer an open question","supersedes":"6eaf389b4d95244b057b96d6aca8d566af0e38fb62482508b6c3cb70cdce7d0c","tags":["claim:faq-open-evolution","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/pages/format.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T19:13:26.828753Z","id":"6f455f54f38ae9a202c08d3c451f135c7e5db7ce18b77345b7b20697e888013f","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"The sentence was reworded to claim nothing measurable (a growing share of the work); the unsourced majority claim is cut (consultant pick 19).","supersedes":"52b17c0a72b8b9928ad69a3642bc388c1741b9233aebae9a6c2b76c5c52ed154","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:a69c02ae-2421-41a9-88c7-35c5942b4c1f"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/pages/format.md","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T14:35:42.262875Z","id":"c7d62eec2a5b4e278200afb7f8d97e999f3af2f1352e15a2b1cef91939df6bd0","body":{"detail":"crates/toolpath/tests/signatures.rs (signed_step_and_path_verify, tampered_change_fails, moved_head_fails_both_path_signatures, missing_required_scope_fails, gpg_and_sigstore_are_not_verified, scopes_without_a_canonical_form_are_refused) and tests/jcs.rs (RFC 8785 reference vectors), feature 'verify' (810a58b): author and reviewer verify; a ci scope is refused (scopes_without_a_canonical_form_are_refused) because the RFC defines no canonical form for it; no producer signs anything. Dropped CI from the claim (consultant pick 17): the ci scope waits for the over proposal.","kind":"pass","span":{"start":{"line":141},"end":{"line":141},"content_hash":"85d1a48e4435d93da8f5d8153a9fe3b091feceb61b27683f0f2dc0bcb17b427f"},"summary":"Format page: scoped signatures author/reviewer: both verify (ssh Ed25519)","supersedes":"2d6d89ad16a32237b1d47816cf5a88aec6b23700946212f5fa0afc04f9a84457","tags":["claim:scoped-signatures","claims","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260","session:claude-code:a69c02ae-2421-41a9-88c7-35c5942b4c1f"]}}
